  "pr_number": 8584,
  "issue_number": 7219,
  "issue_title": "add native support for playwright tracing",
  "issue_body": "### Clear and concise description of the problem\n\nAs a developer using Vitest, I want to be able to easily enable playwright tracing through config file so that I can use it for debugging both local and CI runs.\r\n\r\nCI example: Generate tracing files, upload artifacts to GH actions and generate a [trace.playwright.dev](https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer#viewing-remote-traces) link\r\n\r\nLocal example: Generate tracing files in similar directories to what we currently have for `__screenshots__` but call it `__traces__` instead. Ideally we add a button in vscode extension so we can run `npx playwright show-trace` or open [trace.playwright.dev](https://playwright.dev/docs/trace-viewer#viewing-remote-traces) in browser.\r\n\r\nAnd yes, Im interested in submitting a PR for this issue. I already have code implemented in my project so Im hoping it wont be that hard to move it to vitest and add some tests.\n\n### Suggested solution\n\nAdd following custom commands:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\n/// <reference types=\"@vitest/browser/providers/playwright\" />\r\nimport type { BrowserProvider, BrowserProviderOptions, BrowserCommand } from 'vitest/node'\r\nimport { unlink } from 'node:fs/promises'\r\nimport { basename, dirname, resolve } from 'pathe'\r\n\r\nconst resolveTracesPath = (testPath: string, name: string) => {\r\n  const dir = dirname(testPath)\r\n  const base = basename(testPath)\r\n  return resolve(dir, '__traces__', base, name)\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const getTracingConfig: BrowserCommand<[]> = async context => {\r\n  const provider = context.provider as BrowserProvider & { options: BrowserProviderOptions }\r\n  return provider.options.context?.trace\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const startTracing: BrowserCommand<\r\n  [params: { screenshots?: boolean; snapshots?: boolean }]\r\n> = async (context, params) => {\r\n  if (context.provider.name === 'playwright') {\r\n    await context.context.tracing.start(params)\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  throw new Error(`provider ${context.provider.name} is not supported`)\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const stopTracing: BrowserCommand<[params: { name: string }]> = async (\r\n  context,\r\n  { name }\r\n) => {\r\n  if (!context.testPath) {\r\n    throw new Error(`Cannot record tracing without a test path`)\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (context.provider.name === 'playwright') {\r\n    const path = resolveTracesPath(context.testPath, `${name}.zip`)\r\n    await context.context.tracing.stop({ path })\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  throw new Error(`provider ${context.provider.name} is not supported`)\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const deleteTracing: BrowserCommand<[params: { name: string }]> = async (\r\n  context,\r\n  { name }\r\n) => {\r\n  if (!context.testPath) {\r\n    throw new Error(`Cannot delete tracing without a test path`)\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (context.provider.name === 'playwright') {\r\n    const path = resolveTracesPath(context.testPath, `${name}.zip`)\r\n    await unlink(path).catch(err => {\r\n      if (err.code === 'ENOENT') {\r\n        // Ignore the error if the file doesn't exist\r\n        return\r\n      }\r\n      // Re-throw other errors\r\n      throw err\r\n    })\r\n    return\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  throw new Error(`provider ${context.provider.name} is not supported`)\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nAdd following test hooks:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nimport { beforeEach, afterEach, Task, RunnerTask } from 'vitest'\r\nimport { server } from '@vitest/browser/context'\r\n\r\nconst { getTracingConfig, startTracing, stopTracing, deleteTracing } = server.commands\r\n\r\nconst traceConfig = await getTracingConfig()\r\nconst traceMode = traceConfig?.mode ?? 'off'\r\nconst tracingOptions = {\r\n  screenshots: traceConfig?.screenshots ?? true,\r\n  snapshots: traceConfig?.snapshots ?? true,\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst getName = (task: RunnerTask, forceRetryCount?: number) => {\r\n  const retryCount = forceRetryCount ?? task.result?.retryCount\r\n  const suiteName = task.suite ? `${task.suite.name.replaceAll(' ', '-')}-` : ''\r\n  const taskName = task.name.replaceAll(' ', '-')\r\n  return `${suiteName}${taskName}-${retryCount}`\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (traceMode === 'on') {\r\n  beforeEach(async () => {\r\n    await startTracing(tracingOptions)\r\n  })\r\n  afterEach(async context => {\r\n    const name = getName(context.task)\r\n    await stopTracing({\r\n      name,\r\n    })\r\n  })\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (traceMode === 'retain-on-failure') {\r\n  beforeEach(async () => {\r\n    await startTracing(tracingOptions)\r\n  })\r\n  afterEach(async context => {\r\n    const retryCount = context.task.result?.retryCount ?? 0\r\n    const name = getName(context.task)\r\n    await stopTracing({\r\n      name,\r\n    })\r\n\r\n    if (context.task.result?.state === 'pass') {\r\n      await Promise.all(\r\n        new Array(retryCount + 1).fill(undefined).map((_, index) => {\r\n          const name = getName(context.task, index)\r\n          return deleteTracing({\r\n            name,\r\n          })\r\n        })\r\n      )\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (traceMode === 'on-all-retries') {\r\n  beforeEach(async context => {\r\n    const retryCount = context.task.result?.retryCount\r\n    if (retryCount) {\r\n      await startTracing(tracingOptions)\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n  afterEach(async context => {\r\n    const retryCount = context.task.result?.retryCount\r\n    if (retryCount) {\r\n      const name = getName(context.task)\r\n      await stopTracing({\r\n        name,\r\n      })\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n}\r\n\r\nif (traceMode === 'on-first-retry') {\r\n  beforeEach(async context => {\r\n    const retryCount = context.task.result?.retryCount\r\n    if (retryCount === 1) {\r\n      await startTracing(tracingOptions)\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n  afterEach(async context => {\r\n    const retryCount = context.task.result?.retryCount\r\n    if (retryCount === 1) {\r\n      const name = getName(context.task)\r\n      await stopTracing({\r\n        name,\r\n      })\r\n    }\r\n  })\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nConfig would look like:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ninstances: [\r\n  {\r\n    browser: 'chromium',\r\n    launch: {},\r\n    context: {\r\n      trace: {\r\n        mode: 'on-all-retries',\r\n        screenshots: true,\r\n        snapshots: true,\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n],\r\n```\n\n### Alternative\n\nAdd documentation teaching how to implement it in user land. Without native support it doesnt make sense to add the button to the extension, which would be sad cause being able to run tests from VSCODE and having a button to open the playwright traces for failing tests would be really powerful.\n\n### Additional context\n\nMaybe it makes sense to only enable it in run mode considering the nuances we face with vitest/ui: If we start recording traces after the ui has already loaded, traces will miss css from vitest/ui and will look broken. Also, the right sidebar makes the iframe view really small which is not ideal when debugging traces.\n\n### Validations\n\n- [X] Follow our [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] Read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [X] Read the [docs](https://vitest.dev/guide/).\n- [X] Check that there isn't already an issue that request the same feature to avoid creating a duplicate.",
